Back when I was colorizing PC-HACK 3.0, I experimented with adding a large
zoo level.  There were three rooms: a thin one on the right with the stairs
up, a think one on the left with the stairs down, and a big one in the middle
with lots of stuff, but lots of monsters.  The problem was that it took a
*very* long time to move, with all of those monsters.  I would certainly
like more complex levels, but we have to be careful with the number of
things that happen each turn.

